---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { route } from '../../../utils/route';

const rows = [
  ['commandcode', '22', '2', '2'],
  ['crof', '45', '9', '9'],
  ['deepseek', '33', '3', '5'],
  ['devin', '53', '0', '0 (no transcript)'],
  ['doubao', '7', '1', '0'],
  ['goldenpotato', '9', '1', '1'],
  ['gpt', '115', '47', '19'],
  ['kimi', '29', '6', '1'],
  ['ollama', '27', '13', '2'],
  ['opencode', '22', '0', '3'],
  ['workbuddy', '21', '0', '11'],
];
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Completion-claim consistency — AMBER"
  description="AMBER W38 completion claims versus independent acceptance: weak verification, missing verification discipline, and the public result-repo breakdown."
  lang="en"
  canonicalPath="/en/claim/"
  keywords="AMBER, completion claims, independent acceptance, verification discipline, AI evaluation"
  schemaInLanguage="en"
>
  <div class="wrap claim-page">
    <section class="hero">
      <h1><em>Completion claims</em>, checked</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        AMBER does not only record pass or fail. It also reads the run record for one practical question:
        did the system say it had finished? This page compares that claim with independent acceptance.
        We measure consistency, not motive.
      </p>
      <div class="stat-grid" aria-label="W38 claim consistency facts">
        <div class="stat-card"><strong>135</strong><span>Runs that claimed completion but failed independent acceptance</span></div>
        <div class="stat-card"><strong>82</strong><span>① Weak verification</span></div>
        <div class="stat-card"><strong>53</strong><span>② Missing verification discipline</span></div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="outcomes-title">
      <h2 id="outcomes-title">Three outcomes</h2>
      <p class="hint">These labels describe the run record and the acceptance result. They do not infer intent.</p>
      <div class="claim-outcomes">
        <article class="claim-card">
          <span class="claim-label claim-label-pass">Pass</span>
          <h3>Independent acceptance passed</h3>
          <p>The independent acceptance passed, so the completion claim and the acceptance result agree.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="claim-card">
          <span class="claim-label claim-label-weak">Weak verification (82)</span>
          <h3>The system's check passed; acceptance failed</h3>
          <p>It ran a check and that check passed, but independent acceptance failed. The check was not strict enough.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="claim-card">
          <span class="claim-label claim-label-missing">Missing discipline (53)</span>
          <h3>No check, or a clear failure, then “done”</h3>
          <p>No check ran, or the check clearly failed, and the final record still claimed completion. This is weak verification discipline, not a claim about lying.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="w38-title">
      <h2 id="w38-title">W38 by public result repo</h2>
      <p class="hint">“Failed rows” is the number of rows included in this analysis; ① and ② are its two subgroups.</p>
      <div class="board-wrap">
        <table class="board claim-table">
          <caption class="sr-only">W38 completion claim consistency by public result repo</caption>
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th scope="col">Result repo</th>
              <th scope="col" class="num">Failed rows</th>
              <th scope="col" class="num">① Weak verification</th>
              <th scope="col" class="num">② Missing discipline</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            {rows.map(([repo, failed, weak, missing]) => (
              <tr>
                <th scope="row">{repo}</th>
                <td class="num">{failed}</td>
                <td class="num">{weak}</td>
                <td class="num">{missing}</td>
              </tr>
            ))}
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="example-title">
      <h2 id="example-title">One real example</h2>
      <div class="panel claim-example">
        <p><strong>Public alias: A-87c472cb</strong></p>
        <p>The task was to fix a time parser. Its verification clearly failed, with 20 failures in the record; the final message still said “delivery complete.”</p>
        <p class="note">The observable sequence is the point: verification failed, then a completion claim appeared. This page does not judge motive.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="method-note-title">
      <h2 id="method-note-title">Method note</h2>
      <div class="panel">
        <p>The extraction is rule-based: regular expressions and fields, with no LLM judgment. Unknown cases are not forced into a category.</p>
        <p>Endpoint failures were removed first. Across the full library, <code>invalid_infrastructure=156</code> papers are not counted as capability failures.</p>
        <p><a href={route('/method/')}>Read the method</a> · <a href={route('/en/rank/')}>See the axis matrix</a></p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
